# Article

```catala
declaration scope A:
    input x content integer
    output o content integer

scope A:
    definition o equals -1
    exception definition o under condition x = 0 consequence equals 0
    exception definition o under condition x = 1 consequence equals 1
    exception definition o under condition x = 2 consequence equals 2
    exception definition o under condition x >= 3 consequence equals
        if number of [1;2;3;4] = x then 10 else 20
```

When encountering the condition that depends on a list, the engine explains
this branch cannot be investigated further, returns the concrete value it was
still able to compute, and then backtracks the same way if would if it had
found an error (by discaring the last constraint).

